  {
    "number": 144,
    "title": "Fix ordinary Codex current status across successive turns",
    "body": "Ordinary Codex Desktop hooks report unknown ordering, so successive turns previously left activity unknown and kept the prior completion notice pending. The shared reducer now selects an eligible unseen turn start by receipt order, accepts its matching stop, and clears completion notices only for consumers configured to do so. Provider ordering stays unknown; an unseen delayed start can still select incorrectly.\n\nRefs #137.\n\nThe change preserves independent attention and acknowledgment, bounds retired IDs to 256 with FIFO eviction, and recovers existing ambiguous version 1.0 stores without a reset. Agent-state 2.0.0 and Hub 0.2.0 mark the changed behavior while retaining lifecycle/snapshot/storage 1.0. The actual hook and pinned Pixoo/Nanoleaf consumers are exercised with disposable state and fake physical transports.\n\nValidation: Node 24 build/type; 112 state tests and 70 Hub tests; both-language contracts/lifecycle/state consumers; isolated reproducible packages; MCP, setup, privacy/deadline, performance/isolation, workflow, dashboard/browser and real-consumer checks pass. A frozen pre-change export verifies recovery. The ordinary lifecycle, parent-independence, duplicate-metadata and mixed retirement-bound regressions failed before their fixes. The newly merged bounded cross-device suite also passes all 12 scenarios with successful cleanup. Workflow validates 11 specifications and 12 archived changes.\n\nThe guide inputs/output, state documentation and installed-update runbook are synchronized. Guide generation, five maintenance tests, browser/print and no-drift checks pass. Ownership diagrams retain their existing pins because the change stays inside the same reducer and adds no transport or writer.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification review and all six current-head CI jobs are required before guarded merge. After merged-main checks, publish new immutable archives with checksums/source receipts, close #137, and reconcile confirmed delivery in a linked guide-only completion PR. Public guide publication, installation and the real Desktop/Pixoo retest remain separate; Pixoo #34 owns installed acceptance. Reset #138 and history #139 are excluded.\n\nDelivery uses one coordinating writer and independent read-only reviewers. No live service, personal hook, database or physical device is changed.\n",
    "state": "open",
